IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-absd-spouses`

-- Stamp Duties (Spouses) (Remission of ABSD) Rules 2013 -- worked cases. Expected results written by hand from the text.
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Date
`on` y m d MEANS Date WITH year IS y, month IS m, day IS d

GIVEN r IS A Residence, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Spouse
`a spouse` r n MEANS Spouse WITH residence IS r, `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` IS n

GIVEN x IS A Spouse, y IS A Spouse, `married` IS A BOOLEAN, `executed` IS A Date
GIVETH A Purchase
`a joint purchase by` x y `married` `executed` MEANS
    Purchase WITH
        `number of joint parties` IS 2
        `the parties are married to each other` IS `married`
        `first party` IS x
        `second party` IS y
        `to be held as partnership property` IS FALSE
        `executed on or after 9 May 2022 and to be held on trust` IS FALSE
        `executed on` IS `executed`

-- A completed property (TOP before execution); the old home sold on `sold`, claim made on `claimed`.
GIVEN `sold` IS A Date, `claimed` IS A Date, `still married` IS A BOOLEAN, `bought another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Aftermath
`sold the old home on` `sold` `claimed` `still married` `bought another` MEANS
    Aftermath WITH
        `ABSD paid to the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `TOP or CSC granted on or before the date of execution` IS TRUE
        `earlier of TOP and CSC` IS `sold`
        `every property that made a party an owner has been disposed of` IS TRUE
        `date of the last disposal` IS `sold`
        `either party acquired another residential property before that disposal` IS `bought another`
        `on that date the two own the new property together and with no one else` IS TRUE
        `on that date they remain married` IS `still married`
        `refund claimed on` IS `claimed`
        `the Commissioner allowed a longer period for the claim` IS FALSE

-- An uncompleted property: no TOP or CSC at execution; TOP on `top`.
GIVEN `top` IS A Date, `sold` IS A Date
GIVETH A Aftermath
`bought off plan, TOP on` `top` `sold` MEANS
    Aftermath WITH
        `ABSD paid to the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `TOP or CSC granted on or before the date of execution` IS FALSE
        `earlier of TOP and CSC` IS `top`
        `every property that made a party an owner has been disposed of` IS TRUE
        `date of the last disposal` IS `sold`
        `either party acquired another residential property before that disposal` IS FALSE
        `on that date the two own the new property together and with no one else` IS TRUE
        `on that date they remain married` IS TRUE
        `refund claimed on` IS `sold`
        `the Commissioner allowed a longer period for the claim` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Purchase
`the couple's EC purchase` MEANS
    `a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) TRUE (`on` 2040 4 28)

§ `REQ-0009 (cradle-to-grave-simone e081, alternative ordering)`

-- Two citizens who jointly own their first flat (each "a Singapore citizen owning one property", rule 4(2)(c)) buy a
-- completed resale EC on 28 April 2040 for $1,200,000, paying ABSD at 20% ($240,000) under Article 3(bi). Remitted in full if
-- the flat is sold within 6 months, ABSD is paid, nothing else is bought, they still own the EC together and are still
-- married, and the refund is claimed within 6 months of the sale.
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` `the couple's EC purchase` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `rule 3 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the last day to dispose of the other property` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 10 28) (`on` 2040 11 1) TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS 20401028
#ASSERT `the ABSD remitted` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 10 1) (`on` 2040 11 1) TRUE FALSE) 240000 EQUALS 240000
#ASSERT `the ABSD remitted` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 10 28) (`on` 2040 11 1) TRUE FALSE) 240000 EQUALS 240000
#ASSERT `the ABSD remitted` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 10 29) (`on` 2040 11 1) TRUE FALSE) 240000 EQUALS 0

§ `Rule 4(3)(d), (e), (f) -- the other conditions`

#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 9 1) (`on` 2040 9 2) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 9 1) (`on` 2040 9 2) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 9 1) (`on` 2041 3 1) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2040 9 1) (`on` 2041 3 2) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Rule 4(3)(c)(B) -- an uncompleted property`

-- Bought off plan on 28 April 2040; TOP on 15 March 2043; the old flat must go by 15 September 2043.
#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`bought off plan, TOP on` (`on` 2043 3 15) (`on` 2043 9 15)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `rule 4 remits the ABSD` `the couple's EC purchase` (`bought off plan, TOP on` (`on` 2043 3 15) (`on` 2043 9 16)) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Rule 4(3A) -- 12 months for the 2020 cases`

-- Executed 1 December 2019: six months ends 1 June 2020, on or after 1 February 2020, so 12 months: 1 December 2020.
#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the last day to dispose of the other property` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) TRUE (`on` 2019 12 1)) (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2020 11 30) (`on` 2020 12 1) TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS 20201201
-- Executed 1 June 2019: six months ends 1 December 2019, before 1 February 2020, so 6 months.
#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the last day to dispose of the other property` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) TRUE (`on` 2019 6 1)) (`sold the old home on` (`on` 2019 11 30) (`on` 2019 12 1) TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS 20191201

§ `Month arithmetic`

#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the date months after` (`on` 2040 8 31) 6) EQUALS 20410228
#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the date months after` (`on` 2043 8 31) 6) EQUALS 20440229
#ASSERT `the ordinal of` (`the date months after` (`on` 2040 7 15) 6) EQUALS 20410115

§ `Rule 4(2) -- who is within the rule`

#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) (`a spouse` foreigner 1) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore permanent resident` 0) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` foreigner 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
-- A PR owning none with a foreigner owning one: no description fits (the citizen spouse is essential).
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore permanent resident` 0) (`a spouse` foreigner 1) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Owning two: outside.
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 2) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not married: outside.
#ASSERT `is within rule 4(1)` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 1) FALSE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Rule 3 -- neither owns property`

-- A first-time citizen and a foreign spouse: ABSD (60% for the foreigner under Article 3(bi)) remitted in full at the outset.
#ASSERT `rule 3 remits the ABSD` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) (`a spouse` foreigner 0) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `rule 3 remits the ABSD` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore permanent resident` 0) (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `rule 3 remits the ABSD` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore permanent resident` 0) (`a spouse` foreigner 0) TRUE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `rule 3 remits the ABSD` (`a joint purchase by` (`a spouse` `Singapore citizen` 0) (`a spouse` foreigner 0) FALSE (`on` 2040 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
